Oscilloscope Math demo · 《吉布斯现象》 The Gibbs Phenomenon · third-party assets and sources

## Voice
- Kokoro-82M (hexgrad), voice am_michael, Apache License 2.0; run locally via kokoro-onnx (MIT) through the library's
  core/tts/tts.py. Speech check: faster-whisper base.en (MIT; OpenAI Whisper weights, MIT). Script: demo/voice/lines.json.

## Music samples (CC0; credit not required, given with thanks)
- Versilian Community Sample Library (VCSL, Versilian Studios): vibraphone_bowed, glockenspiel (core/audio/sampler.py).
  The Fourier plucks, the signal tone, the bass, the bells, relays, clicks, sweeps and the power-off are synthesised by
  demo/mix.py and core/audio/sfx.py.

## Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1; licence texts in demo/fonts/)
- JetBrains Mono: The JetBrains Mono Project Authors, https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/jetbrainsmono
- STIX Two Text (roman and italic): The STIX Fonts Project Authors, https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/stixtwotext
- Noto Serif SC: Google / Adobe (Source Han Serif), https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/notoserifsc
  Static instances (and the Chinese subset, renamed "OM Serif SC" inside the file) made by make_fonts.py from the
  variable fonts that build.sh downloads into demo/fonts/src/.

## Code
- Manim Community v0.22.1 (MIT), Cairo renderer, installed into demo/.venv by build.sh.
- MathJax 3.2.2 (npm mathjax-full, Apache License 2.0; its TeX fonts Apache 2.0 / OFL): typeset the formula once into
  demo/tex/formulas.json (demo/tools/tex2svg.mjs); not needed to build.
- OpenCV (Apache 2.0), NumPy (BSD), fontTools (MIT) for the phosphor pass and the fonts.

## Images, models
- None. Every line, circle and letter is drawn by code; no photographs, no external models, no AI-generated images.

